                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "742eee64-fc55-3cb2-ac86-e35c488677be",
                        "entry_id": "635eb889-f2ce-31fa-bef3-ac4afcf3596a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "diminutive of гости́нец (gostínec): little present, gift"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "diminutive",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da816a14-7f73-419c-8828-c253eed702db",
                                "sense_id": "742eee64-fc55-3cb2-ac86-e35c488677be",
                                "text": "— Где же ты? — кри́кнул опя́ть стари́к и вы́сунул ещё бо́льше го́лову, вы́сунул её с плеча́ми, озира́ясь на все сто́роны, напра́во и нале́во, — иди́ сюда́; я гости́нчику пригото́вил, иди́, покажу́!..",
                                "translation": "\"Where are you?\" cried the old man again; and he thrust his head out farther, thrust it out to the shoulders, gazing in all directions, right and left. \"Come here, I've a little present for you. Come, I'll show you...\"",
                                "english": "\"Where are you?\" cried the old man again; and he thrust his head out farther, thrust it out to the shoulders, gazing in all directions, right and left. \"Come here, I've a little present for you. Come, I'll show you...\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
